# [Send a Decision request]($heading.id('decision'))

`POST /v1/systemone` accepts a JSON object and returns scored labels for the
requested questions. The loaded checkpoint must support Decision. Use the
[worked request]($link.page('llmd/decision').ref('send-a-decision-request'))
or copy one from the [quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart').unsafeRef('send-a-decision-request')).

| Request field | Type | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `state` | String or object, required | Input shared by every question. The server renders an object as compact JSON. |
| `questions` | Object, required | Maps question IDs to definitions. IDs must be nonempty and exclude the colon character. Send dependencies before the questions that reference them. |
| `instructions` | String, optional | System instructions shared by all questions. |
| `ask` | Array of question IDs, optional | Select the questions to answer. Include every dependency of the selected questions. Omitting this field asks all questions. |
| `model` | String, optional | The endpoint uses the checkpoint already loaded by LLMD. The field can be omitted. |

# [Question kinds and dependencies]($heading.id('question-kinds-and-dependencies'))

Each question requires `kind` and a string `instructions`. Its `criteria`
describe the possible labels.

| `kind` | `criteria` | Successful `label` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `choice` | Required object mapping labels to descriptions. Use a string or `null` for each description. | One of the object keys. |
| `noul` | Optional object with descriptions under `"true"` and `"false"`. | The string `"true"` or `"false"`. |
| `score` | Required array of scale labels, such as `["low","medium","high"]`. | One of the supplied strings. |

Use `depends_on` to supply a list of earlier question IDs whose available
labels become context. Use `ask_if` to gate execution. Its keys are earlier
question IDs and its values are arrays of acceptable labels. Every named
question must return a label in its corresponding array for the question to run.

# [Read the response]($heading.id('decision-response'))

`answers` maps each requested ID to a result. A successful entry
contains the winning `label`, a `scores` array, and `prompt_contribution`.
Each score gives the label, its first `token_id`, its full-vocabulary
`logprob`, and its `probability` normalized over the offered labels.
`prompt_contribution` is the total probability mass of the offered label
tokens before this normalization. `usage` totals prompt and cached tokens
across the questions that ran.

This illustrative response uses `"ask": ["animal"]` with the guide's
request. Token IDs, counts and scores depend on the tokenizer, model and run.

```json
{
  "answers": {
    "animal": {
      "label": "cat",
      "scores": [
        {"label": "cat", "token_id": 7, "logprob": -0.916291, "probability": 0.8},
        {"label": "dog", "token_id": 9, "logprob": -2.302585, "probability": 0.2}
      ],
      "prompt_contribution": 0.5
    }
  },
  "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 48, "cached_tokens": 0}
}
```

# [Limits and errors]($heading.id('decision-limits-and-errors'))

A false condition produces `{"skipped":true}` for that question.
A question can also return an `error` field with `prompt_too_long`,
`unsupported_chat_template`, `resource_exhausted`, or `aborted`.
Check individual entries even after HTTP 200. An unsupported
model or invalid request produces HTTP 400 with a plain-text explanation.
For `ForwardDependency`, put the referenced question earlier in the JSON
object. For `DuplicateOptionToken`, choose labels whose first tokens differ.

LLMD revision `ca575167` limits the request body to 4 MiB, accepts 1–1,024
questions, and scores 2–16 options per question. Its Decision path is enabled
for the LFM3 model implementation. See the [Decision catalog]($link.page('llmd/models').unsafeRef('decision-checkpoints'))
for checkpoint and build evidence, and [Parallel work and Decision requests]($link.page('llmd/cli/batching-and-memory').ref('parallel-work-and-decision-requests'))
for the per-request concurrency control `--systemone-window`.
